# Narrowed-replay cache: a machine-generated map from mutation label to the test that catches it.
# Disposable by design — deleting it costs one slow run and nothing else, which is exactly why it is
# not committed. `scripts/mutations.ps1` stays hand-curated; this is not.
scripts/mutation-claims.json

# The mutation runner's crash-recovery copies of the files it is mid-way through editing. Same
# reasoning as the cache above: a snapshot of a tree that is deliberately broken right now is not
# source, and committing it captures mutants as if they were the real thing. Its own line, and its
# own paragraph, because a rule appended to the end of a comment is a rule that does not exist.
scripts/.mutation-backup/
